# Expectation record for 08_gcc_extensions/008_inline_asm_per_target.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 008_inline_asm_per_target
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = Inline assembly with operand constraints, guarded per architecture
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Each architecture branch performs the same logical 32-bit integer operation, so the printed
result does not depend on which branch the preprocessor selected.  Every asm statement
declares its outputs, inputs and clobbers truthfully, writes only to objects named as
outputs, and reads only initialized inputs, so no object is modified through an
undeclared path.  All arithmetic stays inside the range of int.
Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
asm_branch_selected=1
asm_folded_add=1037
asm_folded_sub=963
asm_folded_xor=973
asm_folded_sub_neg=-963
asm_folded_xor_neg=-963
asm_runtime_add=1037
asm_runtime_sub=963
asm_runtime_xor=973
asm_runtime_sub_neg=-963
asm_runtime_xor_neg=-963
asm_chain=1936
asm_matches_c=1
END
